<title>GHANA: European Union gives Ghana $147 million in aid.</title>
<headline>European Union gives Ghana $147 million in aid.</headline>
<dateline>ACCRA 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union is to give Ghana a grant of 130 million Ecu ($147 million) to help it improve its transport infrastructure and for rural development, the government said in a statement.</p>
<p>Under the terms of an agreement signed in Accra this week, some 80 percent of the aid will be earmarked for these two priority sectors.</p>
<p>The rest of the money will be used in the fields of health, education and private sector development, the statement said. ($ = 0.88 Ecu)</p>
</text>
